Patch summary:
Restore the guest's push constants after emulated-texture decompression.

When a guest transitions an emulated ETC2/ASTC image to a readable layout,
CompressedImageInfo::decompressIfNeeded() records a compute dispatch that binds
the decompression pipeline and calls vkCmdPushConstants for its parameters.
The barrier handlers already re-bind the guest's compute pipeline and
descriptor sets afterwards, but not its push constants. RADV keeps a single
push constant block per command buffer shared by all bind points, so the
decompression parameters overwrite the guest's graphics push constants (ANGLE's
driver uniforms). ANGLE does not re-push unchanged values within a command
buffer, so the next draw runs with corrupted driver uniforms and produces no
fragments.

Asphalt 8 on x86-64 RADV hosts hits this every time it blends a newly loaded
ASTC vignette mask: the blend is dropped, the mask stays black and the whole
3D scene fades to black under gfxstream_guest_angle and gfxstream.

Track vkCmdPushConstants per command buffer in the global state (routing both
decoders through a new on_vkCmdPushConstants hook) and replay the recorded
writes after every decompression, alongside the existing compute re-bind.
Writes are kept in submission order so overlapping updates replay exactly; a
write is dropped only once a later one covers all of its stages and bytes
(regardless of layout, since ANGLE pushes the same range with per-program
layouts), which keeps the list to one entry per range in practice.

